Step 2: First, we expand the product on the left-hand side of the equation in order to better understand it. Therefore, $x - 4$ times $2y -1$ is equal to $2xy - x - 8y + 4$. Why? Because $x-4$ multiplies with $2y$ as $2xy-4y$, and $x-4$ multiplies with $-1$ as $-x+4$.

