Step 3: Now we will group like terms together in order to find out where to start simplifying the equation. When I group like terms, I get $2xy - x$ on the one side of the equation (these terms are the ones that have a variable x with them) and $- 8y$ and $+4$ on the other side (the terms without variable x; keep in mind that when adding these terms, we should also change the sign). Combine the constant terms though by adding -1 to 4: $- 8y + 4 -1 = - 8y + 3$ because -1 + 4 = 3.

