The volume of the solid base is computed as the sampling area times the height of the base. In our problem, the sampling area is the area of one equilateral triangle (base CB, side CD) with a side of 12 units. The height can be computed as (12/2) giving half the height H divided by the fraction 3/2, so the final computation for expressing the base area is $(12*12*sqrt{3}/4)*((2*12)-16)$: This calculation yields the exact area of base 160 sqrt(3) square units.

