## Step 1: Consider the denominator of the given sum
We start by examining the expression \[1 + \omega^k + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}.\]We notice that this expression can be factored as \[(\omega^k - 1)(\omega^{2k} - 1).\]

## Step 2: Use the factored form to rewrite the sum
Using the factored form of the denominator, we can rewrite the given sum as \begin{align*}
\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1 + \omega^k + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}}
&= \sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{(\omega^k - 1)(\omega^{2k} - 1)}.
\end{align*}

## Step 3: Use partial fractions to simplify the sum
We rewrite each term in the sum as the difference between two partial fractions: \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{(\omega^k - 1)(\omega^{2k} - 1)}
&= \frac{1}{\omega^k - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega^{2k} - 1}.
\end{align*}

## Step 4: Use the differences to telescope the sum
We then rewrite the sum as \begin{align*}
\left( \frac{1}{\omega^1 - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega^2 - 1} \right)
+ \left( \frac{1}{\omega^2 - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega^4 - 1} \right)
+ \dotsb
+ \left( \frac{1}{\omega^{1704} - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega^{1708} - 1} \right)
+ \left( \frac{1}{\omega^{1708} - 1} - \frac{1}{(\omega^{1709} - \omega) (\omega^{1712} - \omega^3)} \right) .
\end{align*}

## Step 5: Notice how most terms in the sum cancel
We notice that all the middle terms of the sum cancel: \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{\omega^2 - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega^4 - 1}
&= \frac{-1}{\omega \left( \omega^2 - 1 \right)},
\end{align*} \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{\omega^4 - 1} - \frac{1}{\omega^8 - 1}
&= \frac{-1}{\omega^2 \left( \omega^4 - 1 \right)},
\end{align*} and so on, which simplifies the sum to \begin{align*}
\frac{1711 \omega}{\omega-1} \text{ unit }
\end{align*}.

## Step 6: Notice that a careless cancellation between terms
When we add the first and last terms, we should notice that \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{\omega - 1} =  \frac{\omega+1}{(\omega-1)( \omega+1) } \text{ unit } .
\end{align*}With 1/\omega+1-1=1.

## Step 7: Simplify finally the sum
So we have \[\boxed{ \frac{1710}{\omega-1} = 1728 \text{ }}\]

